This project follows the memory design of Goose (https://github.com/aardappel/goose):
data stacks, relative references and stack assignment.

Files in bench/ taken from Goose's benchmark suite (Apache License 2.0, see
bench/LICENSE-goose):

  Copied unchanged:
    bench/bench.h, bench/push.goose, bench/rng.goose, bench/bintrees.cpp,
    bench/push.cpp, and (copied in by compare_more.sh) bench/tree.cpp,
    bench/interp.cpp, bench/sexp.cpp

  Modified (benchmark size changed):
    bench/bintrees.goose

  Written for topstack, based on Goose's C++ and Rust versions of the same
  benchmarks (same algorithms, inputs and output):
    bench/bintrees_topstack.cpp, bench/bintrees_ref.cpp, bench/bintrees_thread.cpp,
    bench/bintrees_pmr.cpp, bench/bintrees_llvm.cpp, bench/push_topstack.cpp,
    bench/push_pinned.cpp, bench/tree_topstack.cpp, bench/interp_topstack.cpp,
    bench/sexp_topstack.cpp, bench/bintrees_ref16.cpp, bench/tree_ref16.cpp,
    bench/interp_ref16.cpp, bench/sexp_ref16.cpp, bench/bintrees_protobuf.cpp,
    bench/rust_bumpalo/templates/*.rs, bench/sum_topstack.cpp,
    bench/strlist_topstack.cpp, bench/records_topstack.cpp, bench/graph_topstack.cpp,
    bench/words_topstack.cpp, bench/particles_topstack.cpp, bench/lru_topstack.cpp,
    bench/scene_topstack.cpp, bench/calc_topstack.cpp, bench/respond_topstack.cpp,
    bench/blur_topstack.cpp

The comparison scripts also copy further Goose sources into bench/bin/ at run
time; those copies are not part of this repository.

bench/llvm_shim.cpp was written for topstack, not copied from LLVM. It behaves like
LLVM's allocate_buffer, deallocate_buffer and SmallVectorBase::grow_pod, so the LLVM
benchmark can run without loading libLLVM.
